{"type":"message","id":"455bed11","parentId":"d3c1a8ec","timestamp":"2026-03-16T00:00:24.988Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"이것은 크론 작업으로 실행되는 요청입니다. 매일 09:00 KST 기준으로 GitHub 인기 레포지토리 브리핑을 생성해야 합니다.\n\n요구사항:\n1. GitHub API (gh api 또는 공식 REST)로 실제 데이터 조회\n2. 최근 인기 Top 5 (최근 7일 생성 + stars 기준)\n3. 누적 스타 상위 Top 5 (archived 제외, 최근 활동 있는 레포 우선)\n4. 각 레포 핵심 설명 1~2문장\n5. OpenClaw 또는 Claude Code에 바로 적용 가능한 아이디어 3~5개\n6. 오늘 바로 실행할 액션 3개\n7. 중복 레포는 한 번만 노출\n8. 전체 2500자 이내로 간결하게 작성\n9. 한국어로 전달\n\n현재 시간은 2026-03-16 09:00 KST (2026-03-16 00:00 UTC)\n\n먼저 GitHub API를 사용하여 데이터를 조회해야 합니다. gh 명령어를 사용할 수 있는지 확인하고 실제 데이터를 가져와야 합니다.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"GitHub API를 사용하여 실제 데이터를 조회하겠습니다."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_d706af3b93054831998916fc","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh api search/repositories --field q=created:>=2026-03-09 --field sort=stars --field order=desc --limit 5 --jq '.items[] | {name, full_name, stargazers_count, description, language, created_at, updated_at}'","timeout":30000}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zai","model":"glm-4.7","usage":{"input":13330,"output":677,"cacheRead":7436,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21443,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773619218246}}
{"type":"message","id":"e960af89","parentId":"455bed11","timestamp":"2026-03-16T00:00:25.095Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_d706af3b93054831998916fc","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"unknown flag: --limit\n\nUsage:  gh api <endpoint> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --cache duration        Cache the response, e.g. \"3600s\", \"60m\", \"1h\"\n  -F, --field key=value       Add a typed parameter in key=value format (use \"@<path>\" or \"@-\" to read value from file or stdin)\n  -H, --header key:value      Add a HTTP request header in key:value format\n      --hostname string       The GitHub hostname for the request (default \"github.com\")\n  -i, --include               Include HTTP response status line and headers in the output\n      --input file            The file to use as body for the HTTP request (use \"-\" to read from standard input)\n  -q, --jq string             Query to select values from the response using jq syntax\n  -X, --method string         The HTTP method for the request (default \"GET\")\n      --paginate              Make additional HTTP requests to fetch all pages of results\n  -p, --preview strings       Opt into GitHub API previews (names should omit '-preview')\n  -f, --raw-field key=value   Add a string parameter in key=value format\n      --silent                Do not print the response body\n      --slurp                 Use with \"--paginate\" to return an array of all pages of either JSON arrays or objects\n  -t, --template string       Format JSON output using a Go template; see \"gh help formatting\"\n      --verbose               Include full HTTP request and response in the output\n\n(Command exited with code 1)"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":1,"durationMs":94,"aggregated":"unknown flag: --limit\n\nUsage:  gh api <endpoint> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --cache duration        Cache the response, e.g. \"3600s\", \"60m\", \"1h\"\n  -F, --field key=value       Add a typed parameter in key=value format (use \"@<path>\" or \"@-\" to read value from file or stdin)\n  -H, --header key:value      Add a HTTP request header in key:value format\n      --hostname string       The GitHub hostname for the request (default \"github.com\")\n  -i, --include               Include HTTP response status line and headers in the output\n      --input file            The file to use as body for the HTTP request (use \"-\" to read from standard input)\n  -q, --jq string             Query to select values from the response using jq syntax\n  -X, --method string         The HTTP method for the request (default \"GET\")\n      --paginate              Make additional HTTP requests to fetch all pages of results\n  -p, --preview strings       Opt into GitHub API previews (names should omit '-preview')\n  -f, --raw-field key=value   Add a string parameter in key=value format\n      --silent                Do not print the response body\n      --slurp                 Use with \"--paginate\" to return an array of all pages of either JSON arrays or objects\n  -t, --template string       Format JSON output using a Go template; see \"gh help formatting\"\n      --verbose               Include full HTTP request and response in the output\n\n(Command exited with code 1)","cwd":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1773619225090}}
